---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Psion Organiser II programs
section: psion
description: "Games and utilities for the Psion Organiser II: pack images to download, source, model compatibility and manuals."
---
{% import "components/ui.njk" as ui %}
<div class="wrap psion-list">
  <h1>{{ title }}</h1>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>Games and utilities for the Psion Organiser II, written in OPL and 6303 machine code. Each one comes as a pack image you can run in an emulator or load onto a real Organiser; released programs also come with their source and build as a zip.</p>
    <p>New to this? Start with <a href="/psion/getting-started/">Getting started</a>.</p>
    <p class="hat-tip">A hat tip to Jaap Scherphuis, whose <a href="https://www.jaapsch.net/psion/">Psion Organiser II page</a> inspired these programs: its manuals and technical references made them possible, and his Jape emulator is where every one of them was built and tested.</p>
  </div>
  <nav aria-label="On this page"><ul class="jump">
    <li><a href="#games">Games</a></li>
    <li><a href="#utilities">Utilities</a></li>
    <li><a href="#all-downloads">All downloads</a></li>
  </ul></nav>

  <fieldset class="screen-filter">
    <legend>Show for</legend>
    <input class="sr" type="radio" name="screen" id="scr-all" value="all" checked><label for="scr-all">Every model</label>
    <input class="sr" type="radio" name="screen" id="scr-2" value="2"><label for="scr-2">Two-line <span class="small">CM, XP, LA</span></label>
    <input class="sr" type="radio" name="screen" id="scr-4" value="4"><label for="scr-4">Four-line <span class="small">LZ, LZ64</span></label>
  </fieldset>

  {%- for g in [["games", "Games", "game"], ["utilities", "Utilities", "utility"]] %}
  <h2 id="{{ g[0] }}">{{ g[1] }}</h2>
  <div class="grid">
    {%- for p in collections.programs | byCategory(g[2]) %}
    {{ ui.programCard(p, models_list) }}
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>
  {%- endfor %}

  <hr class="rule">
  <h2 id="all-downloads">All downloads</h2>
  <p class="small">Each program's page has the exact byte counts and SHA-256 checksums.</p>
  <ul class="dl-list">
    {%- for p in collections.programs | withFiles %}
    {%- set newest = p.data.files | newestVersion %}
    <li class="dl-item" data-two="{{ p.data.models | screenSupport(2) }}" data-four="{{ p.data.models | screenSupport(4) }}">
      <div class="dl-what">
        <p class="dl-name"><a href="{{ p.url }}">{{ p.data.title }}</a> <span class="mono small">{{ newest }}</span></p>
        <p class="small">{{ p.data.models | modelsText(models_list) }}{% if p.data.pack %} · {{ p.data.pack }} pack{% endif %} · {% for f in p.data.files %}{% if loop.first %}<time datetime="{{ f.date | dateIso }}">{{ f.date | dateShort }}</time>{% endif %}{% endfor %}</p>
      </div>
      <div class="dl-links">
        {%- for f in p.data.files %}{% if f.version == newest %}
        <a class="chip" href="{{ p.data.downloadDir }}{{ f.file }}" title="{{ f.file }}" download>{{ "Source" if f.kind == "source" else (".opk" if f.kind == "build" else "Organiser files") }}<span class="chip-size">{{ (p.data.downloadDir + f.file) | fileSize | humanSize }}</span><span class="sr">: {{ p.data.title }}, {{ f.file }}</span></a>
        {%- endif %}{% endfor %}
      </div>
    </li>
    {%- endfor %}
  </ul>
</div>
